    historyContent: {
      origins: 'Country/Region of Origin: Province of Brescia, Italy\nTime Period: Historical game with long tradition\nHistorical Development: The game influenced the local card manufacturing tradition, requiring 52-card decks rather than the standard 40-card Italian packs. Related to Scopa and Scopone but with local Bresciane characteristics.\nCultural Significance: The reason Bresciane cards have 52 cards instead of 40. Similar to how Trevisane cards have 52 cards for ScarabociÃ³n.',
