      ],
      timeline: [
        'Historical period: Game develops in Brescia province',
        'Card manufacturing influence: Local decks standardized at 52 cards for Cicera',
        'Present: Continues to be played in Brescia with traditional decks',
      ],
      evolution: 'Cicera evolved from the Scopa family of games, adapting to local preferences and the 52-card Bresciane deck. The game maintains core Scopa mechanics while utilizing the extended deck.',
      cultural: 'The game is deeply connected to Bresciane cultural identity, influencing even the local playing card manufacturing tradition.',
